# Logseq syntax - blocks, refs, properties
# Everything is an outliner block; files stay plain Markdown on disk.
# https://docs.logseq.com/

## References
[[page name]]                    link to (and create) a page
#tag                             same as [[tag]]
#[[multi word tag]]              tag containing spaces
((60a78e9e-59dc-40ab-9a01-...))  block reference - type `((` to search
[label]([[page name]])           page ref with custom display text
[label](((60a78e9e-59dc-...)))   block ref with custom display text
parent/child                     namespace - just a `/` in the page name

## Embeds (transclusion; edits propagate both ways)
{{embed [[page name]]}}          embed a whole page
{{embed ((block-uuid))}}         embed a block and its children
# Embeds do NOT contribute to the source page's linked references.

## Properties - `key:: value`
type:: [[book]]                  block property
tags:: motor, steering wheel     comma-separated values become page refs
description:: "no [[links]]"     quote the value to suppress ref parsing
# Properties in the FIRST block of a page are page properties (frontmatter).
# Names are case-insensitive, lower-cased, and `_` is rewritten to `-`.
# A property with an empty value is neither rendered nor queryable.

## Built-in page properties
title::                    override page title (independent of filename)
alias::                    synonyms; refs to an alias resolve to this page
tags::                     lists page under "Pages tagged with X"
icon::                     page icon
public::                   include in publish/export (boolean)
filters::                  saved linked-reference filters
exclude-from-graph-view::  boolean

## Built-in block properties (Logseq usually writes these for you)
id::                       block UUID - appears when you copy a block ref
collapsed::                boolean
template::                 name that marks this block + children a template
query-table:: query-properties:: query-sort-by:: query-sort-desc::

## Trigger characters
/         slash commands (only at line start or after whitespace)
<         advanced commands - expand to a #+BEGIN_x ... #+END_x section
[[  ((    page / block autocompletion
{{  ::    macro / property autocompletion

## Advanced commands (typed with `<`)
Quote Note Tip Important Caution Warning Example Verse Comment Center
Src      #+BEGIN_SRC clojure ... #+END_SRC       (arg sets the language)
Query    #+BEGIN_QUERY {...} #+END_QUERY         (see logseq/datalog)

## Macros and built-in renderers
{{macro-name arg1, arg2}}   user macro from config.edn :macros
{{query ...}}               simple query           (see logseq/query)
{{function (sum :price)}}   aggregate over the query results above it
{{cards [[Logseq]]}}        flashcard review query
{{cloze answer \\ cue}}     hidden answer; `\\ cue` is optional
{{namespace [[parent]]}}    table of contents for a namespace
{{youtube URL}} {{youtube-timestamp SECONDS}} {{video URL}} {{tweet URL}}

## Media
![](https://host/file.png)               markdown
![](../assets/file.mp4)                  local asset
<video src="..."></video>                raw html also works
[:img {:src "..."}]                      hiccup

## Math (KaTeX)
$inline$
$$display$$

## Templates
template:: meeting-notes             mark the block + children a template
template-including-parent:: false    insert only the children
<% today %> <% yesterday %> <% tomorrow %> <% time %> <% current page %>
<% last friday %>                    natural-language dates (chrono)
# Insert with /Template. Dynamic variables also work inside macros.
